abstract: This English computational laboratory converts umsf-incident-ai-agent 1.0.0
  into a self-contained Google Colab-compatible notebook. It embeds the original source,
  two synthetic incident scenarios and the companion P1 incident fixture. The notebook
  runs 116 original tests without skips and 44 supplied analytical checks, then produces
  30 explanatory figures, an offline interactive replay explorer, CSV/JSON outputs,
  audit evidence and a rendered HTML report. Experiments cover robust personal references,
  missing channels, persistent flags, coverage-aware group decisions, source-qualified
  incident state, exact lexicographic rescue assignment, exact multi-resource service-continuity
  allocation, heuristic recovery scheduling, proposal authority and hash-chain audit
  integrity. Both scenarios are replayed at 41 chronological cutoffs. Deterministic
  algorithms compute all decisions; no external language-model API or credentials
  are required. Every plan remains a proposal. All records are synthetic and the project
  has not been validated against real rescue operations. The original source and localized
  examples are retained verbatim for provenance; the new notebook, figures, explorer
  and documentation are English. All code cells were executed in a fresh local Python/IPython
  process with only the notebook supplied. Hosted Google Colab frontend execution
  and live LLM API compatibility were not directly tested.
keywords:
- critical infrastructure
- incident support
- rescue logistics
